For example, the number 12 equals \(2 \times 2 \times 3\). No other combination of prime factors can produce 12 except the same primes rearranged.

An integer \(n\) is prime if \(n>1\) and its only positive divisors are \(1\) and \(n\). For instance, 7 has exactly these two divisors, so it is prime.

